<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Deliberately empty.

  colorPrimary, colorPrimaryDark and colorAccent are still required — values/styles.xml
  references all three, and without them the resource compiler fails with
  "resource color/colorPrimary not found" and the app cannot be built at all. The
  Capacitor template references these names but never ships their definitions.

  They are now generated from client/brand.properties by `resValue` in
  app/build.gradle rather than fixed here, because they are brand values: the
  in-app UI is themed at runtime from GET /api/branding, so a colour frozen into
  the native shell is one of the few things that CAN visibly clash with the
  college it is running for. They used to be one college's navy (#1a3a8f) and
  maroon (#9e1b32); the defaults are now neutral slate.

  Do not add them back here: a resource declared both here and by resValue is a
  hard build failure ("duplicate value for resource").
-->
<resources>
</resources>
